{"step_index":64,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-18T09:17:59Z","content":"Created At: 2026-10-18T14:47:59+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-10-18T14:48:00+05:30\n\nThe command exited with code 0.\nOutput:\n22-### Turn 2 — Delegation / System Input\r\n23-\r\n24-```xml\r\n25-<codex_delegation>\r\n26-  <source_thread_id>01a060f9-09a3-73f0-8553-999a4a6886a3</source_thread_id>\r\n27:  <input>Add Trading Bot as the fifth business/project idea in this shared Businesses task. The five are now SignalFoundry, Velvet Thread, Mara Veyne, Bubbles, and Trading Bot. Treat Trading Bot as an unscoped idea awaiting owner details; do not connect financial accounts, request credentials, deploy live strategies, or place trades without a specific future request and the required owner approvals.</input>\r\n28-</codex_delegation>\r\n29-```\r\n30-\r\n31-### Turn 3 — Assistant\r\n32-\r\n33:Added Trading Bot as the fifth project. The shared list is now:\r\n34-\r\n35-1. SignalFoundry\r\n36-2. Velvet Thread\r\n37-3. Mara Veyne, including QuickByte\r\n38-4. Bubbles\r\n39:5. Trading Bot — unscoped, awaiting your details\r\n40-\r\n41-No financial account connections, credential requests, live strategy deployments, or trades without your specific request and required approvals.\r\n42-\r\n43-### Turn 4 — Assistant\r\n44-\r\n--\r\n63-\r\n64-### Turn 8 — Assistant\r\n65-\r\n66-Updated: Velvet Thread is now managed through Antigravity and excluded from active work and pending maintenance here. Its existing files, archive, website, and records remain untouched.\r\n67-\r\n68:This main business chat now handles SignalFoundry, Mara Veyne (including QuickByte), Bubbles, and Trading Bot. Velvet Thread returns only if you explicitly bring it back.\r\n69-\r\n70-### Turn 9 — Delegation / System Input\r\n71-\r\n72-```xml\r\n73-<codex_delegation>\r\n--\r\n98-\r\n99-Scope updated:\r\n100-\r\n101-- Velvet Thread is fully managed through Antigravity for now.\r\n102-- Codex will stop all Velvet Thread work—including deployment, development, product additions, store management, and maintenance.\r\n103:- I’ll focus on SignalFoundry, Mara Veyne/QuickByte, Bubbles, and Trading Bot.\r\n104-- The unfinished Cloudflare upload is not deployed or live.\r\n105-\r\n106-Velvet Thread returns here only if you explicitly reassign it.\r\n107-\r\n108-### Turn 13 — Delegation / System Input\r\n--\r\n184-For the other businesses:\r\n185-\r\n186-- SignalFoundry: no—professional services are prohibited.\r\n187-- Mara Veyne: no—digital content and non-material products are prohibited.\r\n188-- Bubbles/comedy brand: no—videos and other digital goods are prohibited.\r\n189:- Trading Bot: no—software, financial services, stocks, and securities are prohibited.  \r\n190-  [Depop prohibited-items policy](https://depophelp.zendesk.com/hc/en-gb/articles/360001792167-What-are-Depop-s-prohibited-items)\r\n191-\r\n192-The practical issue is payment and margin. Sri Lankan sellers would use PayPal and normally pay Depop’s 10% selling fee plus PayPal processing fees. Depop also gives preference to listings near the buyer, so international shipping from Sri Lanka may reduce visibility and competitiveness. [Depop fees](https://depophelp.zendesk.com/hc/en-gb/articles/360001791127-Seller-fees-and-charges), [search-ranking factors](https://depophelp.zendesk.com/hc/en-gb/articles/9422984899985-How-Depop-ranks-search-results-and-recommends-listings)\r\n193-\r\n194-PayPal now says Sri Lankan users can receive cross-border payments after linking an eligible Sampath Bank or Commercial Bank account. That banking and identity setup would remain your responsibility. [PayPal Sri Lanka](https://www.paypal.com/lk/business/banking-partners)\r\n\n"}
